PN,31705
SC,0005
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F317A1786027701
OL,3,CDiscarded SpaceX rocket set to
OL,4,Cunintentionally smash into the moon
OL,6,FWednesday's crash will cause a flash
OL,7,Flasting less than a second and will
OL,8,Flikely be too dim to see, experts say.
OL,10,FHowever, stargazers will be excited to
OL,11,Fknow the stream of ejected material
OL,12,Fcould stretch for several miles into
OL,13,Fspace and remain visible through
OL,14,Ftelescopes for tens of minutes.
OL,16,FBenjamin Fernando, a scientist from
OL,17,FLos Alamos National Laboratory, said
OL,18,Fthe moon's low gravity and lack of
OL,19,Fwind will prevent the dust from
OL,20,Fblowing away.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G5/10
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
