PN,31707
SC,0007
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F317A1786027701
OL,3,CDiscarded SpaceX rocket set to
OL,4,Cunintentionally smash into the moon
OL,6,FThe Danuri orbiter is expected to
OL,7,Fstray within a mile or two of the
OL,8,Frocket just two minutes before it
OL,9,Fcrashes into the moon.
OL,11,FThe abandoned SpaceX rocket segment,
OL,12,Fmeasuring 12 meters and weighing
OL,13,Faround 4,500 kilograms hoisted two
OL,14,Fprivate lunar landers in January last
OL,15,Fyear.
OL,17,FOne of them ` Firefly Aerospace's Blue
OL,18,FGhost ` became the first private
OL,19,Fspacecraft to pull off a fully
OL,20,Fsuccessful lunar touchdown. The other,
OL,21,FJapan-based ispace's lander, wrecked.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G7/10
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
